    <h2>1. Executive Summary & 3-Tier Distributed Architecture</h2>
    <p>
        The Sunrise Dental Clinic Management System is an enterprise-grade, computerized 3-tier distributed appointment and financial management software solution. Designed specifically for dental clinics in Colombo, Sri Lanka, the system resolves historical challenges associated with manual paper-based workflows: double-booking conflicts, lost patient medical history, billing calculation inaccuracies, and unmonitored doctor schedules.
    </p>

    <pre>
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  Tier 1: Desktop Client Layer (Java Swing + FlatLaf UI Theme)                 │
│  • Strictly communicates over HTTP/REST using java.net.http.HttpClient        │
│  • Non-blocking asynchronous threading with SwingWorker for all I/O           │
│  • Token-based session context with zero direct JDBC calls                     │
└───────────────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────┘
                                        │ REST / HTTP (JSON Payloads + Bearer Auth)
                                        ▼
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  Tier 2: REST Application Service Layer (Embedded HttpServer - Port 8089)     │
│  • com.sun.net.httpserver.HttpServer with Executors.newFixedThreadPool(10)     │
│  • Token-based SessionManager (Stateful Auth & Instant Revocation)            │
│  • ReportFactory (Factory Method Design Pattern)                               │
│  • Asynchronous JavaMail Booking Notification Dispatcher                      │
└───────────────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────┘
                                        │ JDBC via PreparedStatement / CallableStatement
                                        ▼
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  Tier 3: Database & Persistence Tier (MySQL / MariaDB via XAMPP)               │
│  • DatabaseConnectionManager (Thread-Safe Singleton Pattern)                  │
│  • Database Trigger: trg_before_insert_appointment (Serial APT-YYYY-XXXX)      │
│  • Stored Procedure: CalculateInvoiceTotal (Consultation Fee + Tariff Cost)    │
│  • Stored Function: CheckDentistAvailability (Conflict Overlap Prevention)    │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
    </pre>

    <h2>2. Data Access Object (DAO) Layer Architecture</h2>
    <p>
        The persistence tier is designed strictly around the <b>Data Access Object (DAO) Pattern</b>, which creates a complete abstraction barrier between domain entities/business logic and raw relational SQL statements.
    </p>

    <table class="data-table">
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th>DAO Interface</th>
                <th>Concrete Implementation</th>
                <th>Database Responsibilities & Operations</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td><code>UserDAO</code></td>
                <td><code>UserDAOImpl</code></td>
                <td>Authenticates staff credentials, verifies cryptographic SHA-256 password hashes, and polymorphically maps user roles (<code>Administrator</code>, <code>Receptionist</code>, <code>DentistUser</code>).</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><code>PatientDAO</code></td>
                <td><code>PatientDAOImpl</code></td>
                <td>Handles patient profile persistence, real-time name and contact filtering, and returning patient identification.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><code>DentistDAO</code></td>
                <td><code>DentistDAOImpl</code></td>
                <td>Maintains clinician directory, medical specializations, and foreign-key links to authenticated system accounts.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><code>TreatmentDAO</code></td>
                <td><code>TreatmentDAOImpl</code></td>
                <td>Performs CRUD operations on the dental procedure tariff catalog and standard price points.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><code>AppointmentDAO</code></td>
                <td><code>AppointmentDAOImpl</code></td>
                <td>Persists appointments, invokes database triggers for auto-numbering, checks dentist schedule availability, and updates clinical diagnoses and doctor notes.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><code>InvoiceDAO</code></td>
                <td><code>InvoiceDAOImpl</code></td>
                <td>Invokes the MySQL stored procedure <code>CalculateInvoiceTotal</code> and manages composed <code>invoice_items</code> records.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><code>ReportDAO</code></td>
                <td><code>ReportDAOImpl</code></td>
                <td>Executes aggregated financial analytics queries for Daily Schedules, Monthly Revenue, and Top Procedures rankings.</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>

    <h3>2.1 Database Trigger, Stored Procedure & Function Integration</h3>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <b>Database Trigger (<code>trg_before_insert_appointment</code>):</b> When a new appointment is registered, the database trigger intercepts the insert, determines the current year, retrieves the sequential counter, and formats an immutable serial number (e.g., <code>APT-2026-0001</code>).
        </li>
        <li>
            <b>Stored Function (<code>CheckDentistAvailability</code>):</b> Before booking confirmation, the system runs <code>SELECT CheckDentistAvailability(?, ?, ?)</code>. If a conflicting appointment with status <code>SCHEDULED</code> or <code>IN PROGRESS</code> exists, the function returns <code>0</code> and blocks double-booking.
        </li>
        <li>
            <b>Stored Procedure (<code>CalculateInvoiceTotal</code>):</b> Executes <code>CALL CalculateInvoiceTotal(?, ?, ?, ?)</code> using <code>CallableStatement</code> to compute standard consultation fee (LKR 1,500.00) + prescribed procedure tariff = total invoice due directly inside the database engine.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <div class="page-break"></div>

    <h2>3. Software Design Patterns Implementation</h2>

    <table class="data-table">
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th>Pattern Category</th>
                <th>Design Pattern</th>
                <th>Concrete Class / Component</th>
                <th>Architectural Benefit & Role</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td><b>Creational</b></td>
                <td><b>Singleton</b></td>
                <td><code>DatabaseConnectionManager</code><br><code>SessionContext</code></td>
                <td>Guarantees a single centralized JDBC connection manager, eliminating connection pool leaks and driver duplication. <code>SessionContext</code> maintains global client token state.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><b>Creational</b></td>
                <td><b>Factory Method</b></td>
                <td><code>ReportFactory</code><br><code>ReportGenerator&lt;T&gt;</code></td>
                <td>Decouples report request routing from concrete report algorithms (Daily Schedule, Revenue Analysis, Top Treatments), allowing seamless future report extension.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><b>Structural</b></td>
                <td><b>Data Access Object (DAO)</b></td>
                <td><code>*DAO</code> &amp; <code>*DAOImpl</code></td>
                <td>Isolates service layers from SQL dialects and database drivers. Enables seamless unit testing through test isolation.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><b>Structural</b></td>
                <td><b>Data Transfer Object (DTO)</b></td>
                <td>Package <code>dental.server.dto.*</code></td>
                <td>Encapsulates request/response data across network boundaries (e.g., <code>LoginRequest</code>, <code>BookAppointmentRequest</code>, <code>UpdateTreatmentRequest</code>).</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><b>Behavioral</b></td>
                <td><b>Polymorphic Strategy</b></td>
                <td><code>User.getMenuItems()</code></td>
                <td>Abstract <code>User</code> class polymorphically overridden by <code>Receptionist</code>, <code>DentistUser</code>, and <code>Administrator</code> to deliver role-specific dashboards.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><b>Behavioral</b></td>
                <td><b>Observer / Listener</b></td>
                <td>Swing Event Model</td>
                <td>Reactive listeners (<code>ActionListener</code>, <code>DocumentListener</code>) trigger real-time search filtering, dynamic dropdown population, and smooth tab switching.</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>4. Exception Handling & Error Recovery Architecture</h2>
    <p>
        The system implements a robust, multi-tier exception handling architecture ensuring that runtime faults never crash the desktop client or corrupt database state.
    </p>

    <pre>
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  Tier 1: Presentation Layer (Java Swing UI)                                    │
│  • SwingWorker.done() catches ExecutionException and unwrap cause               │
│  • Displays field-level inline alerts & non-blocking warning popups           │
└───────────────────────────────────────▲────────────────────────────────────────┘
                                        │ HTTP Response JSON (4xx / 5xx Status Code)
                                        │ {"success": false, "error": "...", "statusCode": 409}
┌───────────────────────────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  Tier 2: REST HTTP Handler Layer (RestHandler)                                 │
│  • Centralized try-catch pipeline wrapping all request dispatches              │
│  • Domain Exception to HTTP Status Code Mapping:                               │
│      - ValidationException         ──> HTTP 400 Bad Request                    │
│      - AuthenticationException     ──> HTTP 401 Unauthorized                   │
│      - ResourceNotFoundException   ──> HTTP 404 Not Found                      │
│      - DoubleBookingException      ──> HTTP 409 Conflict                       │
│      - Unhandled Server Exceptions ──> HTTP 500 Internal Server Error          │
└───────────────────────────────────────▲────────────────────────────────────────┘
                                        │ Throws Checked Domain Exceptions
┌───────────────────────────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  Tier 3: Service & Persistence Layer (JDBC / MySQL)                            │
│  • Try-with-resources blocks guarantee Connection & Statement closure          │
│  • Catches SQLExceptions, logs stack traces via java.util.logging.Logger       │
│  • Safe transaction rollback on failure                                        │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
    </pre>

    <h3>4.1 Custom Domain Exception Hierarchy</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><b><code>ValidationException</code> (HTTP 400):</b> Thrown when input data fails business validation (e.g. invalid phone number, empty patient name, past appointment date).</li>
        <li><b><code>AuthenticationException</code> (HTTP 401):</b> Thrown on invalid login credentials or expired/missing Bearer session tokens.</li>
        <li><b><code>ResourceNotFoundException</code> (HTTP 404):</b> Thrown when querying nonexistent appointment serial numbers (e.g. <code>APT-9999-9999</code>) or deleted records.</li>
        <li><b><code>DoubleBookingException</code> (HTTP 409):</b> Thrown when the database detects overlapping doctor appointment slots, returning clear conflict feedback.</li>
        <li><b><code>ApiException</code>:</b> Client-side exception wrapper encapsulating network disconnects and HTTP error payloads.</li>
    </ul>

